  <div class="post-content"><p>Welcome to my blog.</p>
<h1 id="ayesha-here-aka-eivrach">Ayesha Here! aka Eivrach.<a hidden class="anchor" aria-hidden="true" href="#Ayesha-here-aka-eivrach">#</a></h1>
<p><strong>I’m a passionate technology enthusiast who loves learning about programming, problem-solving, and how things work behind the scenes in the world of computing. This blog is my space to document what I learn and share useful insights with others who are also curious about technology.</strong></p>
<hr>
<ul>
<li>Currently a student at <strong>FAST-NUCES</strong>, diving deep into the world of computer science, systems, and problem-solving.</li>
<li>Also part of <strong>CoLab</strong>, a research lab where innovation, learning, and curiosity drive the work we do.</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h2 id="-what-youll-find-here">🛠️ What You&rsquo;ll Find Here?<a hidden class="anchor" aria-hidden="true" href="#-what-youll-find-here">#</a></h2>
<p>On this site, you will find content related to my journey in learning technology and computer science. I share new technologies and problem-solving approaches that help make technical topics easier to understand. I am also enthusiastic about <strong>tech</strong>, <strong>Linux</strong>, <strong>coding</strong>, and the tools that make all of it just a bit more efficient.</p>
<p>Most of what I write is rooted in hands-on learning—small guides, notes, and how-to.</p>
<hr>
<h2 id="stack">Stack<a hidden class="anchor" aria-hidden="true" href="#stack">#</a></h2>
<p>Here are some of the tools and technologies I frequently work with :</p>
<p><strong>Git | GitHub | Linux | Ubuntu | C | C++ | OOP | Slack | JavaScript | HTML | CSS | Hugo | VS Code | LinkdIn</strong></p>
<hr>
<h2 id="why-this-blog-exists">Why This Blog Exists?<a hidden class="anchor" aria-hidden="true" href="#why-this-blog-exists">#</a></h2>
<p>I’ve always found that writing clarifies thinking. This space helps me document what I learn and share it in a way that’s helpful to anyone walking a similar path—especially those who enjoy working with systems, code, and clean command lines.</p>
<p>You won’t find fluff here—just honest breakdowns of what works (and sometimes what doesn’t).</p>
<hr>
